00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:56.740
episode

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:56.740
"Fersen,

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:56.740
a Farewell Rondeau"

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:33.800
There's nothing in particular I wanted
to speak to you about.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:37.560
I just figured it would be good practice
to bout with you once in a while.

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:42.300
Thank you.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:44.120
I broke a good sweat out there.

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:51.210
Come to think of it, André...

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:53.580
You once talked about some cheap bar in Paris.

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:54.880
Will you take me there?

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.090
Let's have a drink for once.

00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:01.090
Fersen.

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:03.020
They're preparing your dinner, as well.

00:04:03.020 --> 00:04:04.640
Why don't you stay a little longer?

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:07.420
Thank you, but no. Perhaps some other time.

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:18.070
Taking him to a cheap bar in
Paris is out of the question.

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:20.170
The Count will be thrown out of his seat...

00:04:20.170 --> 00:04:22.940
...and be kicked out of the
bar in less than five minutes.

00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:28.780
The entire city is talking about it.

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:33.020
Queen Marie Antoinette and her
fine-looking lover from Sweden.

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:36.150
An illicit love affair, burning with
passion in Versailles every night.

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:39.430
The rumor has taken a life of its own and
is spreading with wild exaggerations.

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:42.450
The way Count Fersen was acting today...

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:44.130
I've never seen him like that before.

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:46.030
No matter what he did....

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:49.060
...he seemed tormented, but on the other hand, he had to try...

00:04:49.670 --> 00:04:53.030
If his love is that tormenting,
why did he get so involved?

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:08.220
What's so hard about loving and being loved?

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:12.180
There are plenty of loves that can't
even be confessed in this world.

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:16.130
Grab your sword, André.

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:16.870
To the backyard.

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:27.470
André!

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:28.680
No holding back today!

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:30.850
Fine with me!

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:32.640
I wasn't planning on holding
back either today, Oscar.

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:51.640
<i>Oscar!</i>

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:52.740
<i>Forget about him!</i>

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:54.670
<i>Forget about Fersen!</i>

00:05:54.670 --> 00:05:57.410
<i>No, I want you to forget him...</i>

00:05:57.410 --> 00:05:58.430
<i>Please...</i>

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:03.250
This one measly drink.

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:05.180
This is my life.

00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:07.220
No love, no romance.

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:10.190
This is what I get for breaking my back all day.

00:06:10.190 --> 00:06:13.490
This one measly drink.

00:06:14.530 --> 00:06:16.150
This is my life.

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:19.060
No love, no romance.

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:23.100
The only things I have are
debts and a starving family.

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:24.690
That's all I have.

00:06:25.270 --> 00:06:27.740
Who cares about Versailles.

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:29.810
A princess from Austria?

00:06:29.810 --> 00:06:33.280
A dangerous liaison with a Swedish noble?

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:35.550
We wouldn't know.

00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:38.980
We couldn't care less about Versailles.

00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:43.590
All we want is one measly drink.

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:45.750
One measly drink...

00:06:48.830 --> 00:06:53.000
Just wait and see what'll happen
at the luncheon today,

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:55.470
between ''you know who'' and ''you know who.''

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:03.470
Well, well, it's finally time for her entrance.

00:07:04.780 --> 00:07:06.150
See? Here she comes.

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:13.250
Welcome to the luncheon.

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:14.960
Everyone, please enjoy yourselves.

00:07:23.930 --> 00:07:27.510
Watch, she'll approach Count Fersen now.

00:07:32.770 --> 00:07:34.570
Who does she think she's fooling?

00:07:34.570 --> 00:07:37.910
There isn't a soul in Versailles, or even all
of France, that doesn't know about them.

00:07:42.150 --> 00:07:45.380
<i>Fersen, I'll see you at Le Temple de L'Amour tonight.</i>

00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:46.820
<i>You remember, don't you?</i>

00:07:47.180 --> 00:07:48.390
<i>Of course.</i>

00:07:48.390 --> 00:07:50.680
<i>No matter what happens, I'll be there!</i>

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:02.160
So, what did Her Majesty do?

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:04.470
That's it.

00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:06.670
She didn't exchange a word with Lord Fersen.

00:08:07.240 --> 00:08:08.870
Of course, she didn't.

00:08:08.870 --> 00:08:10.710
She has her position to consider.

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:11.740
If His Majesty were to find out—

00:08:11.740 --> 00:08:13.760
Shh! You're speaking too loudly!

00:08:18.980 --> 00:08:21.060
Have you called for me, Your Majesty?

00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:22.720
You two.

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:24.060
Leave us.

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:25.250
Certainly.

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:40.490
You're the only person who
I can count on, Oscar...

00:08:42.010 --> 00:08:44.710
You'll listen to my request, won't you?

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:48.010
Plus, you're the only person
who will keep it a secret.

00:08:49.110 --> 00:08:52.970
Please... convey this to him in secret...

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:55.450
I won't be able to go tonight.

00:08:55.450 --> 00:09:00.830
I had forgotten His Majesty's
friend is visiting tonight.

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:04.800
I have to entertain him all night
long along with His Majesty.

00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:09.440
Please convey to him that I'm sorry...
from the bottom of my heart...

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:12.400
Please say yes, Oscar...!

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:16.740
If you don't, I won't be able to
raise my face and look at you.

00:09:23.550 --> 00:09:25.620
<i>Please raise your face.</i>

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:28.950
<i>How could I ever refuse Your Majesty's request?</i>

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:35.430
<i>Oh, Oscar... You really are the only one.</i>

00:09:35.430 --> 00:09:39.260
<i>Amid all the terrible gossipers,
you're my only ally.</i>

00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:48.530
Oscar, what was Her Majesty's request?

00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:51.340
Hey, Oscar!

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:51.940
What's the matter?

00:09:55.410 --> 00:09:56.110
Oscar!

00:09:56.110 --> 00:09:57.150
Go back without me!

00:09:57.150 --> 00:09:58.240
I'll be home later!

00:10:14.030 --> 00:10:15.120
"Your Majesty."

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:17.970
"With all due respect, I must offer you my opinion."

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:24.600
"Your Majesty, have you forgotten your
position as Queen, Mother of France?"

00:10:26.380 --> 00:10:28.980
"Asking a lowly subject like me for a favor..."

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:32.720
"...while covering your face,
as though you were a sinner..."

00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:35.210
"I understand Your Majesty's pain."

00:10:36.020 --> 00:10:37.590
"However, Your Majesty...!"

00:10:37.590 --> 00:10:38.990
"You have your position to consider!"

00:10:39.890 --> 00:10:42.330
Stop it... Oscar...

00:10:42.330 --> 00:10:45.960
What is there to say...
To those who love each other...?

00:10:57.580 --> 00:10:58.410
Oscar!

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:04.580
And then, she mentioned...

00:11:04.580 --> 00:11:07.850
...of how she's looking forward
to the ball next week.

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:10.810
Thank you, Oscar.

00:11:13.120 --> 00:11:14.230
See you then.

00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:14.860
Wait, Oscar!

00:11:15.100 --> 00:11:16.590
Come in and warm yourself!

00:11:16.590 --> 00:11:17.870
Stay until the rain stops!

00:11:19.460 --> 00:11:20.590
Oscar...

00:11:31.750 --> 00:11:32.500
Oscar!

00:11:33.110 --> 00:11:35.010
You shouldn't be out in the rain like this!

00:11:58.220 --> 00:12:00.380
It's hopeless now.

00:12:01.160 --> 00:12:02.780
There's no turning back.

00:12:03.620 --> 00:12:06.660
The agony of a man who picked a rose.

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:08.830
A bottle of wine.

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:10.530
Ceaseless rain.

00:12:10.530 --> 00:12:12.630
The agony only worsens.

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:16.200
Yet, the Seine flows as usual today.

00:12:17.910 --> 00:12:18.870
Lord Fersen.

00:12:19.440 --> 00:12:21.480
What will you be wearing to tonight's ball?

00:12:21.480 --> 00:12:25.470
Will it be the military uniform or
the formal wear with the crest?

00:12:26.780 --> 00:12:28.920
There's still time until evening.

00:12:28.920 --> 00:12:29.880
I'll decide later.

00:12:29.880 --> 00:12:32.090
Yes, certainly.

00:12:32.090 --> 00:12:33.420
Please excuse me.

00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:52.540
Oscar François, what do you think?

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:54.440
What should I do from here on out?

00:12:58.110 --> 00:13:00.980
Step right up, step right up!
The new installment is on sale!

00:13:00.980 --> 00:13:03.350
This one's a little expensive though.

00:13:03.350 --> 00:13:06.690
From ''The Naked Queen
Seducing Fersen'' series!

00:13:06.690 --> 00:13:10.490
Step right up! Part two covers the romance
between the Austrian and the Swede...

00:13:10.490 --> 00:13:13.550
...that has disgraced our France!
Part two is on sale now!

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:16.230
Come in.

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:19.540
Lord Fersen, a message has
just arrived from our homeland.

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:20.790
A message...?!

00:13:20.790 --> 00:13:26.600
Count Lindesberry, your classmate from Royal
Stockholm University, has passed away.

00:13:27.270 --> 00:13:28.900
It says he died in battle.

00:13:29.500 --> 00:13:30.840
Died in battle?!

00:13:30.840 --> 00:13:34.540
He was fighting in the war for
independence in America.

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:42.390
<i>During this time, across the Atlantic Ocean in America,</i>

00:13:42.390 --> 00:13:46.090
<i>a war was being waged for
independence from England.</i>

00:13:46.090 --> 00:13:48.530
<i>Allying themselves with America,</i>

00:13:48.530 --> 00:13:51.850
<i>France recruited soldiers and sent
them as Expeditionary Forces.</i>

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:08.250
André.

00:14:08.250 --> 00:14:09.620
There's no need to ready the carriage.

00:14:11.320 --> 00:14:13.290
I'm not going to the ball tonight.

00:14:13.850 --> 00:14:16.290
If anyone asks, I'm bedridden with a fever.

00:14:16.820 --> 00:14:17.810
Understand?

00:14:19.390 --> 00:14:20.090
Oscar!

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:22.330
Don't shout.

00:14:22.330 --> 00:14:23.630
You'll scare the horses.

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:28.590
Tonight is the grand ball, where almost all
\hthe prominent nobles will be in attendance.

00:14:29.370 --> 00:14:32.270
If the heir to the Jarjayes family and Regiment
Commander of the Royal Guards,

00:14:32.270 --> 00:14:35.010
Oscar François de Jarjayes, isn't in attendance,

00:14:35.010 --> 00:14:36.610
something out of order is bound to happen, I think.

00:14:37.510 --> 00:14:39.600
I can't bear it, especially because it's the grand ball!

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:44.470
Lady Antoinette will be the target of countless
snide remarks and the people's vulgar stares.

00:14:44.470 --> 00:14:46.570
I can't bear to see her like that.

00:14:47.420 --> 00:14:48.390
That's exactly why!

00:14:48.390 --> 00:14:50.540
That's exactly why you should go,
don't you think?

00:14:51.290 --> 00:14:53.560
You're the only one Lady Antoinette
can depend on.

00:14:53.560 --> 00:14:55.500
Most likely, for Fersen, as well.

00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:58.460
I want no part of it!

00:14:59.570 --> 00:15:02.130
Their business is theirs. Not mine.

00:15:03.100 --> 00:15:05.170
What do you expect me to do?!

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:07.570
Slay the insolent gossipers?!

00:15:07.570 --> 00:15:10.090
Blind the eyes of those who stare?!

00:15:11.880 --> 00:15:12.810
Good idea{There's an idea for you}.

00:15:12.810 --> 00:15:13.550
Let's give it a shot.

00:15:50.020 --> 00:15:52.850
Oscar, is it all right if we go faster?
We're running a little late!

00:15:53.210 --> 00:15:54.390
Yeah.

00:15:55.160 --> 00:15:56.850
All right, go!

00:15:59.310 --> 00:16:03.300
Is that the lady-killer from Sweden?

00:16:03.300 --> 00:16:06.070
Indeed, look at that smug look on his face.

00:16:06.070 --> 00:16:09.740
He probably thinks there isn't a man who's
more handsome than him in this world.

00:16:10.370 --> 00:16:13.270
How did he attract the Queen's affections?

00:16:14.170 --> 00:16:16.200
Oh, oh! What's he looking for?

00:16:16.710 --> 00:16:18.440
No surprise there.

00:16:28.050 --> 00:16:29.960
My, what a wonderful dress.

00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:31.830
She made sure she looked perfect, didn't she?

00:16:31.830 --> 00:16:34.340
After all, she's dressed to
please Lord Fersen alone.

00:16:50.780 --> 00:16:51.650
It suits you.

00:16:51.650 --> 00:16:52.530
You look splendid.

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:06.790
My, Lady Oscar is wearing
the formal dress uniform.

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:09.630
I've never seen Lady Oscar in her dress uniform!

00:17:09.630 --> 00:17:11.550
My, how dashing!

00:17:12.030 --> 00:17:16.730
Oh, but if she's wearing the dress uniform,
that means she's going to dance tonight.

00:17:16.730 --> 00:17:18.260
That's right.

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:20.630
She's never cared to dance before.

00:17:20.630 --> 00:17:22.900
I'll have to ask her to dance with me. I must!

00:17:22.900 --> 00:17:24.480
Oh, I get to ask her first!

00:17:30.340 --> 00:17:31.610
Oscar.

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:34.380
To what new wind do we owe
this pleasant surprise tonight?

00:17:34.380 --> 00:17:37.050
You've never cared to dance before.

00:17:37.050 --> 00:17:42.110
With all due respect, the wind blows
from the west and also from the east.

00:17:43.920 --> 00:17:46.590
Will your dance partner be a man?

00:17:46.590 --> 00:17:48.040
Or will it be a woman?

00:17:49.130 --> 00:17:51.960
Whatever you wish, Your Majesty.

00:17:59.170 --> 00:18:02.430
However, please allow me to be
your only partner tonight.

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:05.300
Very well.

00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:56.430
Stop, stop...

00:19:01.900 --> 00:19:03.410
Thank you, Oscar.

00:19:03.410 --> 00:19:06.170
If you didn't appear in your dress uniform,

00:19:06.170 --> 00:19:09.430
I would have danced the night away
with Lady Antoinette for certain.

00:19:10.640 --> 00:19:13.410
When I see her, I can't help
but want to dance with her.

00:19:13.410 --> 00:19:18.150
If I had danced with her, my hidden feelings would
undoubtedly have become obvious to others.

00:19:18.150 --> 00:19:23.020
I came dangerously close to dragging
her into another scandal.

00:19:26.830 --> 00:19:30.860
I knew I shouldn't have gone to
the ball, but I still went anyway.

00:19:30.860 --> 00:19:33.360
My thoughtlessness can be blamed for everything.

00:19:34.230 --> 00:19:37.370
If I'm truly capable of loving someone,

00:19:37.370 --> 00:19:40.280
I should have been more
mindful about her position.

00:19:40.810 --> 00:19:44.240
Loving her was permissible, but I never
should have let it become romantic!

00:19:50.020 --> 00:19:54.630
I've caused her to suffer deeply...
unspeakably deeply...

00:19:56.630 --> 00:19:59.840
There's only one thing I can do now.

00:20:01.060 --> 00:20:04.390
I choose to be a coward in her eyes!

00:20:08.570 --> 00:20:10.570
Oscar, I'm going to run away.

00:20:10.570 --> 00:20:12.110
I'm sorry, but I must!

00:20:12.110 --> 00:20:13.940
To a far off place, thousands of miles away!

00:20:19.680 --> 00:20:22.050
Please take care of Lady Antoinette!

00:20:26.550 --> 00:20:27.620
Fersen!

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:28.240
Where are you going?!

00:20:32.490 --> 00:20:33.710
Fersen!

00:20:54.820 --> 00:20:56.080
America, huh...

00:20:56.080 --> 00:20:57.650
What a bold decision he's made.

00:20:58.250 --> 00:21:00.190
Aren't you going to see him off?

00:21:00.190 --> 00:21:02.110
The Expeditionary Force is departing today.

00:21:14.170 --> 00:21:19.010
Colonel Hans Axel von Fersen
of the Swedish Light Dragoon,

00:21:19.010 --> 00:21:21.340
has volunteered for the
Expeditionary Force to America.

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:24.610
Appointed as Marquis La Fayette's
lieutenant commander,

00:21:24.610 --> 00:21:29.980
he is scheduled to board Battleship Jason
and set sail from the Port of Brest today.

00:21:32.690 --> 00:21:35.210
If time allows, please convey this to him.

00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:38.190
I wish him to fight
courageously on the battlefield,

00:21:38.190 --> 00:21:39.950
to achieve victory,

00:21:41.290 --> 00:21:43.570
and to return safely...

00:22:04.120 --> 00:22:07.530
Oh, shoot... I just remembered,
I have to change the horses' shoes today.

00:22:22.540 --> 00:22:24.400
Don't die, Fersen...

